VALUES ('a6ba6d2b-04d2-4b7f-954a-dc7dd59ec504', 'cka-storage-advanced-troubleshooting', 'CKA Practice: Storage & Advanced Troubleshooting', 'kubernetes', ARRAY['CKA', 'Storage', 'PersistentVolumes', 'Troubleshooting']::TEXT[], 38, 'advanced', true, 5, 60, 1, 0);

-- ── Section: Storage: Volumes, Claims & Access Modes (12 questions) — Storage — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Persistent Volumes, Storage Classes, Volume concepts) and the current CNCF CKA exam curriculum's Storage domain; verified via web search against current Kubernetes docs, not copied from any official CNCF exam material. ──

VALUES ('2da59c0c-b5c3-4268-b279-13d98fc5a36b', 'a6ba6d2b-04d2-4b7f-954a-dc7dd59ec504', 1, 'Which PersistentVolume access mode allows the volume to be mounted read-write by multiple Pods across multiple nodes simultaneously?', 'Storage', 'PV Access Modes', 'mcq');
VALUES ('2da59c0c-b5c3-4268-b279-13d98fc5a36b', '539e9f08-36a9-493c-b2b2-d51bf97e3157', 'ReadWriteMany (RWX) permits read-write mounting by many Pods on many nodes at once; this requires a volume backend that actually supports concurrent multi-node writes (e.g. NFS-backed or certain CSI drivers).', 'Storage — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Persistent Volumes, Storage Classes, Volume concepts) and the current CNCF CKA exam curriculum''s Storage domain; verified via web search against current Kubernetes docs, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

VALUES ('6213fd28-4b9d-4718-aceb-594532f843c4', 'a6ba6d2b-04d2-4b7f-954a-dc7dd59ec504', 2, 'How does the ReadWriteOncePod access mode differ from ReadWriteOnce?', 'Storage', 'ReadWriteOncePod', 'mcq');
VALUES ('6213fd28-4b9d-4718-aceb-594532f843c4', '5864a0f7-1e39-4ea1-8f4e-2ba2a17a09ba', 'ReadWriteOnce (RWO) restricts mounting to a single node, but multiple Pods co-located on that node could still mount it. ReadWriteOncePod (GA since Kubernetes v1.29, CSI-only) tightens this to exactly one Pod cluster-wide.', 'Storage — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Persistent Volumes, Storage Classes, Volume concepts) and the current CNCF CKA exam curriculum''s Storage domain; verified via web search against current Kubernetes docs, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

VALUES ('5f79f8a8-856c-465b-9d97-662c6cf868eb', 'a6ba6d2b-04d2-4b7f-954a-dc7dd59ec504', 3, 'Setting a PersistentVolume''s volumeMode to ''Block'' instead of the default ''Filesystem'' means:', 'Storage', 'volumeMode', 'mcq');
VALUES ('5f79f8a8-856c-465b-9d97-662c6cf868eb', '59f47acf-9214-4222-a704-e6b9b390d312', 'volumeMode: Block skips the filesystem layer entirely, exposing a raw block device to the container — used by applications (e.g. some databases) that manage their own storage layout.', 'Storage — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Persistent Volumes, Storage Classes, Volume concepts) and the current CNCF CKA exam curriculum''s Storage domain; verified via web search against current Kubernetes docs, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

VALUES ('453fb7fa-e399-4c68-94dd-1f2731cce922', 'a6ba6d2b-04d2-4b7f-954a-dc7dd59ec504', 4, 'When statically provisioning storage, which fields must an administrator set directly on the PersistentVolume object?', 'Storage', 'Static Provisioning', 'mcq');
VALUES ('453fb7fa-e399-4c68-94dd-1f2731cce922', '62091e91-c9bb-4c45-9d0a-27704a7d255f', 'Static provisioning means an admin creates the PV directly with its capacity, accessModes, and a concrete volume source; a separately-created PVC then binds to it based on matching criteria.', 'Storage — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Persistent Volumes, Storage Classes, Volume concepts) and the current CNCF CKA exam curriculum''s Storage domain; verified via web search against current Kubernetes docs, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

VALUES ('ab3f3b9e-fd9a-415a-bdf2-dcdbf7587687', 'a6ba6d2b-04d2-4b7f-954a-dc7dd59ec504', 5, 'What is the default persistentVolumeReclaimPolicy for a PersistentVolume created via dynamic provisioning?', 'Storage', 'Reclaim Policy', 'mcq');
VALUES ('ab3f3b9e-fd9a-415a-bdf2-dcdbf7587687', 'acd5d835-8841-48fa-b067-ee59f5936925', 'Dynamically-provisioned PVs default to reclaimPolicy: Delete — when the bound PVC is deleted, the PV and its underlying storage are deleted too, unless the StorageClass or PV was configured otherwise.', 'Storage — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Persistent Volumes, Storage Classes, Volume concepts) and the current CNCF CKA exam curriculum''s Storage domain; verified via web search against current Kubernetes docs, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

VALUES ('baed106a-9d6e-42f2-a44a-c6d33b2200ec', 'a6ba6d2b-04d2-4b7f-954a-dc7dd59ec504', 6, 'With reclaimPolicy: Retain, what happens to a PersistentVolume after its bound PersistentVolumeClaim is deleted?', 'Storage', 'Reclaim Policy — Retain', 'mcq');
VALUES ('baed106a-9d6e-42f2-a44a-c6d33b2200ec', '5b9f447b-9c26-4d89-a99e-69ff27bea298', 'Retain preserves the PV''s data for manual recovery. The PV transitions to Released — its data is intact, but Kubernetes won''t automatically rebind it to a new PVC.', 'Storage — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Persistent Volumes, Storage Classes, Volume concepts) and the current CNCF CKA exam curriculum''s Storage domain; verified via web search against current Kubernetes docs, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

VALUES ('2e89e09b-27db-43e1-840f-f98acad60f48', 'a6ba6d2b-04d2-4b7f-954a-dc7dd59ec504', 7, 'A Retain-policy PV is stuck in the Released phase after its PVC was deleted. To make it bindable again for a new PVC, what does an admin typically need to do?', 'Storage', 'Reusing a Released PV', 'mcq');
VALUES ('2e89e09b-27db-43e1-840f-f98acad60f48', '14e978f3-970d-400d-8a84-fd58d5e62637', 'A Released PV retains a stale claimRef pointing at the deleted PVC. An admin must manually edit the PV to clear claimRef (and handle the retained data appropriately) before it becomes Available again.', 'Storage — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Persistent Volumes, Storage Classes, Volume concepts) and the current CNCF CKA exam curriculum''s Storage domain; verified via web search against current Kubernetes docs, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

VALUES ('cad347bc-9025-4aad-ba78-e4b1e518491b', 'a6ba6d2b-04d2-4b7f-954a-dc7dd59ec504', 8, 'For the control plane to bind a PersistentVolumeClaim to a specific pre-existing PersistentVolume, which of the following must hold?', 'Storage', 'PV-PVC Binding', 'mcq');
VALUES ('cad347bc-9025-4aad-ba78-e4b1e518491b', '8a44b41d-bcd3-47a8-a065-4d775399bfe1', 'Binding requires sufficient capacity, compatible access modes, and a matching storageClassName (plus any selector/label requirements) — not an exact capacity match or matching names.', 'Storage — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Persistent Volumes, Storage Classes, Volume concepts) and the current CNCF CKA exam curriculum''s Storage domain; verified via web search against current Kubernetes docs, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

VALUES ('1831ac6e-34ec-418b-8560-70e0249a92db', 'a6ba6d2b-04d2-4b7f-954a-dc7dd59ec504', 9, 'A Pod fails to start with an event reading: ''Multi-Attach error for volume ... Volume is already exclusively attached to one node and can''t be attached to another''. What is the most likely cause?', 'Storage', 'Multi-Attach Error', 'mcq');
VALUES ('1831ac6e-34ec-418b-8560-70e0249a92db', 'fbd1ab8f-6a88-495f-9c75-421031d881d2', 'RWO volumes can only be attached to one node at a time. This error commonly appears during a Pod reschedule where the old node hasn''t released the attachment yet.', 'Storage — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Persistent Volumes, Storage Classes, Volume concepts) and the current CNCF CKA exam curriculum''s Storage domain; verified via web search against current Kubernetes docs, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

VALUES ('af203aa1-f93a-44ca-bdb8-9659162bdf9b', 'a6ba6d2b-04d2-4b7f-954a-dc7dd59ec504', 10, 'What does specifying subPath in a container''s volumeMount allow you to do?', 'Storage', 'subPath', 'mcq');
VALUES ('af203aa1-f93a-44ca-bdb8-9659162bdf9b', '9316addb-fce5-4b3e-8060-176815e10222', 'subPath lets a container mount a sub-path inside a volume — useful for sharing a single volume across containers where each needs only a specific file or directory.', 'Storage — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Persistent Volumes, Storage Classes, Volume concepts) and the current CNCF CKA exam curriculum''s Storage domain; verified via web search against current Kubernetes docs, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

VALUES ('c5aa295d-9275-4a9f-afbf-2dda739a09b8', 'a6ba6d2b-04d2-4b7f-954a-dc7dd59ec504', 11, 'How does a generic ephemeral volume (a Pod''s volumes[].ephemeral field) differ from a plain emptyDir volume?', 'Storage', 'Generic Ephemeral Volumes', 'mcq');
VALUES ('c5aa295d-9275-4a9f-afbf-2dda739a09b8', '8f115ff5-66db-45a9-8684-ae6f3f59463b', 'Generic ephemeral volumes get a real, auto-created PVC (deleted with the Pod), letting Pod-lifecycle-scoped storage use any StorageClass/CSI driver, unlike emptyDir''s plain node-local storage.', 'Storage — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Persistent Volumes, Storage Classes, Volume concepts) and the current CNCF CKA exam curriculum''s Storage domain; verified via web search against current Kubernetes docs, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

VALUES ('5e199b75-3897-4996-9b11-df4b517d8499', 'a6ba6d2b-04d2-4b7f-954a-dc7dd59ec504', 12, 'When a StatefulSet defines volumeClaimTemplates, what happens to the PVCs it creates when the StatefulSet is scaled down, if persistentVolumeClaimRetentionPolicy isn''t set to Delete for whenScaled?', 'Storage', 'StatefulSet volumeClaimTemplates', 'mcq');
VALUES ('5e199b75-3897-4996-9b11-df4b517d8499', 'a5f34c53-9c37-4fb1-8e0f-9d77c0eb3090', 'By default (or with whenScaled: Retain), volumeClaimTemplates-created PVCs survive scale-down, preserving per-ordinal data for when that replica is recreated. persistentVolumeClaimRetentionPolicy (stable since v1.32) lets you opt into Delete instead.', 'Storage — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Persistent Volumes, Storage Classes, Volume concepts) and the current CNCF CKA exam curriculum''s Storage domain; verified via web search against current Kubernetes docs, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

-- ── Section: Storage: Dynamic Provisioning & StorageClasses (10 questions) — Storage — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Persistent Volumes, Storage Classes, Volume concepts) and the current CNCF CKA exam curriculum's Storage domain; verified via web search against current Kubernetes docs, not copied from any official CNCF exam material. ──

VALUES ('8e8cd8ee-8339-4094-8daf-4177ec8c7d9e', 'a6ba6d2b-04d2-4b7f-954a-dc7dd59ec504', 13, 'Which API group/version defines the StorageClass resource?', 'Storage', 'StorageClass API', 'mcq');
VALUES ('8e8cd8ee-8339-4094-8daf-4177ec8c7d9e', '594cd900-ac42-4b82-8a7a-a19fb902bb4d', 'StorageClass is defined under the storage.k8s.io/v1 API group, alongside related storage resources like VolumeAttachment and CSIDriver.', 'Storage — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Persistent Volumes, Storage Classes, Volume concepts) and the current CNCF CKA exam curriculum''s Storage domain; verified via web search against current Kubernetes docs, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

VALUES ('49e94614-1da1-43d9-9479-3d9f43c253cc', 'a6ba6d2b-04d2-4b7f-954a-dc7dd59ec504', 14, 'Setting a StorageClass''s volumeBindingMode to WaitForFirstConsumer instead of the default Immediate means:', 'Storage', 'volumeBindingMode', 'mcq');
VALUES ('49e94614-1da1-43d9-9479-3d9f43c253cc', '1405c954-7ddf-454c-93ba-a31195ca096e', 'WaitForFirstConsumer defers binding/provisioning until a consuming Pod exists, allowing topology-aware placement (e.g. provisioning in the same availability zone the Pod actually lands in).', 'Storage — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Persistent Volumes, Storage Classes, Volume concepts) and the current CNCF CKA exam curriculum''s Storage domain; verified via web search against current Kubernetes docs, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

VALUES ('b5623599-fb81-4428-a4ae-0e9e9ad3c73e', 'a6ba6d2b-04d2-4b7f-954a-dc7dd59ec504', 15, 'A StorageClass has allowVolumeExpansion: false. What happens if you edit a bound PVC''s spec.resources.requests.storage to a larger value?', 'Storage', 'allowVolumeExpansion', 'mcq');
VALUES ('b5623599-fb81-4428-a4ae-0e9e9ad3c73e', 'b2e177ee-20e8-420a-9ca2-839c82bffebb', 'Volume expansion is gated by the StorageClass''s allowVolumeExpansion field; without it set to true, edits to a PVC''s requested size don''t trigger resizing.', 'Storage — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Persistent Volumes, Storage Classes, Volume concepts) and the current CNCF CKA exam curriculum''s Storage domain; verified via web search against current Kubernetes docs, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

VALUES ('6c2d8bd9-966c-4f87-87c7-f06e53a5789c', 'a6ba6d2b-04d2-4b7f-954a-dc7dd59ec504', 16, 'For a StorageClass that does support volume expansion, which resize direction is supported by editing the PVC''s requested storage size?', 'Storage', 'Volume Expansion Direction', 'mcq');
VALUES ('6c2d8bd9-966c-4f87-87c7-f06e53a5789c', 'fbe0966f-9da6-400e-b1ff-6ae1e18b3678', 'Kubernetes volume expansion only supports increasing size; there is no supported mechanism to shrink a PVC''s storage request in place.', 'Storage — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Persistent Volumes, Storage Classes, Volume concepts) and the current CNCF CKA exam curriculum''s Storage domain; verified via web search against current Kubernetes docs, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

VALUES ('43cecb6c-2d86-4032-9c77-f3d519ef08a2', 'a6ba6d2b-04d2-4b7f-954a-dc7dd59ec504', 17, 'A cluster has a StorageClass annotated storageclass.kubernetes.io/is-default-class: ''true''. What happens when a PVC is created without specifying storageClassName?', 'Storage', 'Default StorageClass', 'mcq');
VALUES ('43cecb6c-2d86-4032-9c77-f3d519ef08a2', '8e370ba1-d4a4-48ce-9ab8-830c5aed0472', 'An admission controller applies the annotated default StorageClass to any PVC that omits storageClassName, so provisioning proceeds normally through that class''s provisioner.', 'Storage — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Persistent Volumes, Storage Classes, Volume concepts) and the current CNCF CKA exam curriculum''s Storage domain; verified via web search against current Kubernetes docs, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

VALUES ('caf61d46-d173-4024-85f0-6c6ca11b4a6a', 'a6ba6d2b-04d2-4b7f-954a-dc7dd59ec504', 18, 'A PVC is created with storageClassName left unset, and the cluster has NO StorageClass marked as default. What happens?', 'Storage', 'PVC with No Default StorageClass', 'mcq');
VALUES ('caf61d46-d173-4024-85f0-6c6ca11b4a6a', '6d3814ea-f18f-4d09-b723-c5cd106fc5f4', 'With no default StorageClass, an unset storageClassName behaves like an empty string — the PVC can only bind to a classless, statically-provisioned PV, and otherwise remains Pending indefinitely.', 'Storage — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Persistent Volumes, Storage Classes, Volume concepts) and the current CNCF CKA exam curriculum''s Storage domain; verified via web search against current Kubernetes docs, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

VALUES ('e12e23c0-337f-4c85-b023-d41a30079a11', 'a6ba6d2b-04d2-4b7f-954a-dc7dd59ec504', 19, 'In a StorageClass definition, what does the provisioner field specify?', 'Storage', 'Provisioner Field', 'mcq');
VALUES ('e12e23c0-337f-4c85-b023-d41a30079a11', '481aa777-abf3-4cc5-89ab-604afee251a0', 'provisioner names the plugin (typically a CSI driver such as ebs.csi.aws.com) that dynamically creates storage when a PVC requests this class.', 'Storage — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Persistent Volumes, Storage Classes, Volume concepts) and the current CNCF CKA exam curriculum''s Storage domain; verified via web search against current Kubernetes docs, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

VALUES ('461680b6-55b8-409a-9ffa-0f92248a0e4f', 'a6ba6d2b-04d2-4b7f-954a-dc7dd59ec504', 20, 'What is the primary role of a CSI (Container Storage Interface) driver in modern Kubernetes storage?', 'Storage', 'CSI Drivers', 'mcq');
VALUES ('461680b6-55b8-409a-9ffa-0f92248a0e4f', 'c59cc640-a85d-46ad-be84-e339f119c746', 'CSI decouples storage-vendor logic from Kubernetes core, letting new storage backends be supported as out-of-tree drivers rather than requiring changes to Kubernetes itself.', 'Storage — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Persistent Volumes, Storage Classes, Volume concepts) and the current CNCF CKA exam curriculum''s Storage domain; verified via web search against current Kubernetes docs, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

VALUES ('cfdafee9-c0c9-48a5-a4d6-ee6c8ab32b36', 'a6ba6d2b-04d2-4b7f-954a-dc7dd59ec504', 21, 'Which of the following PVC spec fields is generally immutable after creation (cannot be edited on an existing PVC)?', 'Storage', 'PVC Immutable Fields', 'mcq');
VALUES ('cfdafee9-c0c9-48a5-a4d6-ee6c8ab32b36', '0a949fc7-bdc4-43d5-9f3a-36c14d9783f7', 'A PVC''s accessModes and volumeMode are fixed at creation; only resources.requests.storage can be changed afterward (and only to increase it, if the StorageClass permits expansion).', 'Storage — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Persistent Volumes, Storage Classes, Volume concepts) and the current CNCF CKA exam curriculum''s Storage domain; verified via web search against current Kubernetes docs, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

VALUES ('368d5346-3d58-4e5a-9b3a-ec8fe55ab851', 'a6ba6d2b-04d2-4b7f-954a-dc7dd59ec504', 22, 'A ''local'' PersistentVolume (using volume source local:) ties storage to a specific node''s disk. What must typically accompany it so Pods are only scheduled to that node?', 'Storage', 'Local PersistentVolumes', 'mcq');
VALUES ('368d5346-3d58-4e5a-9b3a-ec8fe55ab851', '4456af3f-9c9f-48be-9777-6e18ce613b72', 'Because local volumes only exist on one node''s disk, the PV must declare a nodeAffinity so the scheduler places consuming Pods on that exact node.', 'Storage — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Persistent Volumes, Storage Classes, Volume concepts) and the current CNCF CKA exam curriculum''s Storage domain; verified via web search against current Kubernetes docs, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

-- ── Section: Advanced Troubleshooting (16 questions) — Troubleshooting — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Debug Pods/Nodes/Cluster, kubeadm cluster administration) and the current CNCF CKA exam curriculum's Troubleshooting domain; verified via web search, not copied from any official CNCF exam material. ──

VALUES ('ca6917bb-73d8-4e42-9e30-e52c98bea1c0', 'a6ba6d2b-04d2-4b7f-954a-dc7dd59ec504', 23, 'A PVC has been stuck in Pending state for several minutes. Which is the most useful first diagnostic command?', 'Troubleshooting', 'PVC Stuck Pending', 'mcq');
VALUES ('ca6917bb-73d8-4e42-9e30-e52c98bea1c0', '1bf679d2-c109-4b7f-8a7f-74b4b443e24c', 'PVCs, like Pods, surface Events explaining scheduling/binding failures via kubectl describe — this is the fastest path to the actual root cause.', 'Troubleshooting — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Debug Pods/Nodes/Cluster, kubeadm cluster administration) and the current CNCF CKA exam curriculum''s Troubleshooting domain; verified via web search, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

VALUES ('430f971e-e2f3-4b22-b064-0f1556bf7ee3', 'a6ba6d2b-04d2-4b7f-954a-dc7dd59ec504', 24, 'A container''s status shows ''Last State: Terminated, Reason: OOMKilled''. What does this specifically mean?', 'Troubleshooting', 'OOMKilled', 'mcq');
VALUES ('430f971e-e2f3-4b22-b064-0f1556bf7ee3', '181170d4-47c7-48c6-a2a0-26f00756dcc9', 'OOMKilled indicates the Linux out-of-memory killer terminated the process, typically because the container hit its memory limit or the node itself was under memory pressure.', 'Troubleshooting — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Debug Pods/Nodes/Cluster, kubeadm cluster administration) and the current CNCF CKA exam curriculum''s Troubleshooting domain; verified via web search, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

VALUES ('a37b876f-dd40-4a12-a1b1-d8b32ec1df10', 'a6ba6d2b-04d2-4b7f-954a-dc7dd59ec504', 25, 'Under node-level MemoryPressure, when the kubelet needs to evict Pods to reclaim resources, which Pods does it generally evict first?', 'Troubleshooting', 'Node Memory Pressure Eviction', 'mcq');
VALUES ('a37b876f-dd40-4a12-a1b1-d8b32ec1df10', 'ac95e33b-da3d-4d4a-9e8e-b08fe1673e50', 'Kubelet eviction ordering follows QoS class: BestEffort Pods are evicted first, then Burstable Pods using more than their requests, and Guaranteed Pods last.', 'Troubleshooting — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Debug Pods/Nodes/Cluster, kubeadm cluster administration) and the current CNCF CKA exam curriculum''s Troubleshooting domain; verified via web search, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

VALUES ('0fd2ff6c-1906-4304-aaca-b3b7e7e92dd0', 'a6ba6d2b-04d2-4b7f-954a-dc7dd59ec504', 26, 'A Pod stays Pending, and ''kubectl describe pod'' shows a FailedScheduling event: ''0/3 nodes are available: 3 Insufficient cpu.'' What does this indicate?', 'Troubleshooting', 'Insufficient CPU Scheduling Failure', 'mcq');
VALUES ('0fd2ff6c-1906-4304-aaca-b3b7e7e92dd0', '968e2d42-946d-42bb-a0d4-3c993478da47', 'This message means the scheduler evaluated all 3 nodes and found none with enough unreserved CPU capacity to satisfy the Pod''s resources.requests.cpu.', 'Troubleshooting — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Debug Pods/Nodes/Cluster, kubeadm cluster administration) and the current CNCF CKA exam curriculum''s Troubleshooting domain; verified via web search, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

VALUES ('52fe7abe-1c8c-4512-974e-6061adf7b869', 'a6ba6d2b-04d2-4b7f-954a-dc7dd59ec504', 27, 'A Pod requires a node affinity rule with requiredDuringSchedulingIgnoredDuringExecution matching a label no node currently has. What happens?', 'Troubleshooting', 'Node Affinity Scheduling Failure', 'mcq');
VALUES ('52fe7abe-1c8c-4512-974e-6061adf7b869', '9b862927-6bdf-4aba-83b7-55f5b3ca2a58', 'requiredDuringSchedulingIgnoredDuringExecution is a hard constraint; if no node satisfies it, the Pod simply cannot be scheduled and stays Pending.', 'Troubleshooting — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Debug Pods/Nodes/Cluster, kubeadm cluster administration) and the current CNCF CKA exam curriculum''s Troubleshooting domain; verified via web search, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

VALUES ('b777c514-e5e2-4cd0-bf8f-437bb089bc96', 'a6ba6d2b-04d2-4b7f-954a-dc7dd59ec504', 28, 'A node has a taint key=value:NoSchedule, and a Pod has no matching toleration. What''s the effect on that Pod''s scheduling to that node?', 'Troubleshooting', 'Taint Without Toleration', 'mcq');
VALUES ('b777c514-e5e2-4cd0-bf8f-437bb089bc96', '21d6a766-f694-456f-871f-d9f35148a93b', 'NoSchedule prevents new Pods without a matching toleration from being scheduled to the tainted node; it does not evict existing Pods (that''s NoExecute''s behavior).', 'Troubleshooting — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Debug Pods/Nodes/Cluster, kubeadm cluster administration) and the current CNCF CKA exam curriculum''s Troubleshooting domain; verified via web search, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

VALUES ('7b70aa86-595d-4e94-9a9c-d4abb7717ae8', 'a6ba6d2b-04d2-4b7f-954a-dc7dd59ec504', 29, 'Which of the following is NOT a typical root cause of a Pod stuck in ImagePullBackOff?', 'Troubleshooting', 'ImagePullBackOff Root Causes', 'mcq');
VALUES ('7b70aa86-595d-4e94-9a9c-d4abb7717ae8', '2aad667c-1d89-439d-9e8c-a7ef95bafe04', 'Memory limits affect runtime OOM behavior, not image pulling. Typos, missing pull secrets, and registry unavailability/rate-limiting are the classic ImagePullBackOff causes.', 'Troubleshooting — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Debug Pods/Nodes/Cluster, kubeadm cluster administration) and the current CNCF CKA exam curriculum''s Troubleshooting domain; verified via web search, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

VALUES ('e4239271-032a-48b9-9e87-893183951445', 'a6ba6d2b-04d2-4b7f-954a-dc7dd59ec504', 30, 'What''s the relationship between the ErrImagePull and ImagePullBackOff states seen in kubectl get pods?', 'Troubleshooting', 'ErrImagePull vs ImagePullBackOff', 'mcq');
VALUES ('e4239271-032a-48b9-9e87-893183951445', '8fc0ad72-8cfb-4802-bd9c-38deb4523736', 'ErrImagePull reports an individual failed pull; if it keeps failing, the kubelet enters an exponential backoff loop shown as ImagePullBackOff.', 'Troubleshooting — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Debug Pods/Nodes/Cluster, kubeadm cluster administration) and the current CNCF CKA exam curriculum''s Troubleshooting domain; verified via web search, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

VALUES ('5dee00f9-89d5-4834-98bc-c498026ce4da', 'a6ba6d2b-04d2-4b7f-954a-dc7dd59ec504', 31, 'When kubectl describe pod''s Events section doesn''t give enough detail about a scheduling or runtime failure, what''s the most direct way to inspect the full resource state as Kubernetes stored it?', 'Troubleshooting', 'Structured Troubleshooting', 'mcq');
VALUES ('5dee00f9-89d5-4834-98bc-c498026ce4da', '83ec616c-737a-4966-80c8-e19c17eb2b2f', '-o yaml/-o json dumps the raw object, including status fields and conditions that describe''s human-readable summary may compress or leave out.', 'Troubleshooting — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Debug Pods/Nodes/Cluster, kubeadm cluster administration) and the current CNCF CKA exam curriculum''s Troubleshooting domain; verified via web search, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

VALUES ('0534bfd2-3b23-427e-b55a-a549255c82f2', 'a6ba6d2b-04d2-4b7f-954a-dc7dd59ec504', 32, 'A Deployment''s Pods use podAntiAffinity with requiredDuringSchedulingIgnoredDuringExecution to avoid co-locating replicas on the same node. What happens when you scale the Deployment beyond the number of available nodes?', 'Troubleshooting', 'Anti-Affinity Scheduling Failure', 'mcq');
VALUES ('0534bfd2-3b23-427e-b55a-a549255c82f2', '7a24ce8b-ab1f-40ff-8b0f-f8a31a21383d', 'A ''required'' anti-affinity rule is a hard constraint; once every node hosts one matching Pod, no node remains valid for further replicas, so they stay Pending.', 'Troubleshooting — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Debug Pods/Nodes/Cluster, kubeadm cluster administration) and the current CNCF CKA exam curriculum''s Troubleshooting domain; verified via web search, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

VALUES ('35e42cca-ed52-4e75-a60d-10ead582ef10', 'a6ba6d2b-04d2-4b7f-954a-dc7dd59ec504', 33, 'You suspect etcd is unhealthy and it''s causing slow kube-apiserver responses cluster-wide. Which command directly checks etcd''s own health/latency?', 'Troubleshooting', 'etcd Health Troubleshooting', 'mcq');
VALUES ('35e42cca-ed52-4e75-a60d-10ead582ef10', '882bc9a1-0d9b-49cd-a47a-95e740a3ddd5', 'etcdctl talks to etcd directly and reports endpoint health/latency; kubectl-level commands don''t give this level of etcd-internal detail.', 'Troubleshooting — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Debug Pods/Nodes/Cluster, kubeadm cluster administration) and the current CNCF CKA exam curriculum''s Troubleshooting domain; verified via web search, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

VALUES ('ae137dbf-e783-4865-a338-4e0fcf0fb516', 'a6ba6d2b-04d2-4b7f-954a-dc7dd59ec504', 34, 'Pods across the cluster suddenly can''t resolve any Service DNS names, though they could earlier. Beyond checking the Pod''s own resolv.conf, what''s a key cluster-level thing to check?', 'Troubleshooting', 'CoreDNS Troubleshooting', 'mcq');
VALUES ('ae137dbf-e783-4865-a338-4e0fcf0fb516', '7ea7d11a-b8ed-477c-9cc0-bb8413f92b1d', 'A cluster-wide DNS outage points at the CoreDNS Deployment itself — check its Pods'' status and logs before assuming a per-Pod configuration issue.', 'Troubleshooting — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Debug Pods/Nodes/Cluster, kubeadm cluster administration) and the current CNCF CKA exam curriculum''s Troubleshooting domain; verified via web search, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

VALUES ('24839362-94bd-4d97-bef9-4e6d08f8dc70', 'a6ba6d2b-04d2-4b7f-954a-dc7dd59ec504', 35, 'A Service exists and its selector matches Pod labels correctly, but clients still can''t reach it. What''s a good next diagnostic step, beyond checking the Service''s Endpoints/EndpointSlice?', 'Troubleshooting', 'Service Not Routing Traffic', 'mcq');
VALUES ('24839362-94bd-4d97-bef9-4e6d08f8dc70', '8565791d-32a1-4d45-aed5-9130d7e52235', 'Matching labels alone doesn''t guarantee traffic flows — readiness gates Endpoints membership, and kube-proxy must be functioning to actually program the routing rules.', 'Troubleshooting — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Debug Pods/Nodes/Cluster, kubeadm cluster administration) and the current CNCF CKA exam curriculum''s Troubleshooting domain; verified via web search, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

VALUES ('3fffe203-3598-4dc8-8256-27a88cdbdabe', 'a6ba6d2b-04d2-4b7f-954a-dc7dd59ec504', 36, 'On a kubeadm-provisioned node running a systemd-managed kubelet, which command shows the kubelet''s own logs for deep node-level troubleshooting (not container logs)?', 'Troubleshooting', 'kubelet Node-Level Logs', 'mcq');
VALUES ('3fffe203-3598-4dc8-8256-27a88cdbdabe', '352ddb1d-ff4f-4eb5-b904-8025b26cd4cf', 'The kubelet itself typically runs as a systemd unit, not a Pod, so its logs are accessed via journalctl -u kubelet on the node, not via kubectl logs.', 'Troubleshooting — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Debug Pods/Nodes/Cluster, kubeadm cluster administration) and the current CNCF CKA exam curriculum''s Troubleshooting domain; verified via web search, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

VALUES ('b241752e-931d-459a-82d7-fb17055c03c9', 'a6ba6d2b-04d2-4b7f-954a-dc7dd59ec504', 37, 'kubectl-level commands aren''t giving enough detail about why a container keeps failing on a specific node. What''s crictl used for in this situation?', 'Troubleshooting', 'crictl for Runtime-Level Debugging', 'mcq');
VALUES ('b241752e-931d-459a-82d7-fb17055c03c9', '7e473e7a-e499-49d1-a18f-3de213650552', 'crictl is a CLI for the Container Runtime Interface, letting you inspect containers/images/pods directly on a node''s runtime (containerd, CRI-O) independent of the API server.', 'Troubleshooting — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Debug Pods/Nodes/Cluster, kubeadm cluster administration) and the current CNCF CKA exam curriculum''s Troubleshooting domain; verified via web search, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');

VALUES ('ab6f95e3-4156-4e8e-b9a7-671e8883c355', 'a6ba6d2b-04d2-4b7f-954a-dc7dd59ec504', 38, 'kubectl commands suddenly start failing cluster-wide with an error like ''x509: certificate has expired or is not yet valid'', and no recent config changes were made. What''s a likely cause worth checking first?', 'Troubleshooting', 'Certificate Expiry Failures', 'mcq');
VALUES ('ab6f95e3-4156-4e8e-b9a7-671e8883c355', '1f66c9bb-6011-4706-a4ca-12556338c9bf', 'kubeadm-generated certificates have a 1-year default validity; expiry (or major clock skew, since x509 validation is time-based) is the classic cause of this exact error appearing cluster-wide.', 'Troubleshooting — authored from kubernetes.io documentation (Debug Pods/Nodes/Cluster, kubeadm cluster administration) and the current CNCF CKA exam curriculum''s Troubleshooting domain; verified via web search, not copied from any official CNCF exam material.');
